1
00:00:00,567 --> 00:00:07,033
[BRIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:13,433 --> 00:00:15,267
Good morning!

3
00:00:15,267 --> 00:00:17,067
Come on, let's eat.

4
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:19,300
Here. I'll serve you.

5
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:23,467
[BRIGHT MUSIC CONTINUES]

6
00:00:23,467 --> 00:00:24,467
I'll do it.

7
00:00:26,667 --> 00:00:28,033
Why?

8
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:32,533
You also like leftover rice?

9
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:35,300
[JUNE] Nice.

10
00:00:36,333 --> 00:00:39,267
Hey! Save some for me!

11
00:00:39,267 --> 00:00:41,200
- Wait.
- Hey!

12
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:42,567
- You're selfish!
- Stop!

13
00:00:42,567 --> 00:00:44,600
Hey! I want some too!

14
00:00:50,067 --> 00:00:51,333
<i> Oh my god!</i>

15
00:00:51,333 --> 00:00:54,167
<i>I hope my hair doesn't
smell like tocino.</i>

16
00:00:56,367 --> 00:01:03,333
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

17
00:01:10,267 --> 00:01:17,267
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

18
00:01:18,400 --> 00:01:19,367
[MUSIC STOPS]

19
00:01:19,367 --> 00:01:22,767
Hey! That's mine!

20
00:01:26,067 --> 00:01:27,467
My brother also likes
leftover rice.

21
00:01:27,467 --> 00:01:30,700
Back then, he'd only steal
leftover rice.

22
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:33,233
- But now--
- You have a brother?

23
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:37,600
Good for you.
I'm an only child.

24
00:01:38,467 --> 00:01:39,667
Are you two close?

25
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:45,600
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

26
00:01:45,633 --> 00:01:47,267
Here.

27
00:01:47,267 --> 00:01:50,633
Ima-Asim Homemade Vinegar.
At your service.

28
00:01:50,633 --> 00:01:52,700
I'll give you even though you
took my leftover rice.

29
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:00,433
If you make a sour face,
you're mine.

30
00:02:06,567 --> 00:02:11,233
[QUIRKY MUSIC PLAYING]

31
00:02:11,233 --> 00:02:12,200
[JUNE] Hmm?

32
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:15,400
It's sour, isn't it?

33
00:02:16,900 --> 00:02:20,233
Hey! That's cheating!

34
00:02:20,233 --> 00:02:24,533
I told you that the<i> tocino</i> and
vinegar complement each other.

35
00:02:24,533 --> 00:02:25,833
Just like us.

36
00:02:25,833 --> 00:02:30,500
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

37
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,367
We both grew up poor.

38
00:02:33,433 --> 00:02:36,533
The only difference is that
I have a bigger family,

39
00:02:36,533 --> 00:02:38,833
so I don't always have
enough money.

40
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,833
It's not your job
to take care of them.

41
00:02:44,733 --> 00:02:47,167
You're teaching them to be
dependent on you,

42
00:02:47,200 --> 00:02:49,800
and that's why you couldn't
get ahead in life.

43
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:56,767
No one else would help us...

44
00:02:57,500 --> 00:02:59,133
so we depend
on each other.

45
00:03:00,533 --> 00:03:04,233
It's useless getting rich
by myself.

46
00:03:06,233 --> 00:03:09,300
I'd rather not get rich if it
means turning back on family.

47
00:03:10,700 --> 00:03:16,267
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]
